s.","short_summary":"A Muir commuter lounge with desks, a quiet room, and hydration station.","evidence_claim":"UC San Diego identifies Muir Commuter Lounge “El Portal” north of Middle of Muir and lists couches, study tables, desks, a quiet room, and a hydration station.","source_url":"https://students.ucsd.edu/campus-services/parking-transportation/commuter/lounges.html","source_title":"Commuter Lounges","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-05-11","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Commuter lockers are available to rent quarterly; confirm current access details with Commuter Services.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ucsd-sixth-commuter-center","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Sixth College Commuter Center","title":"Sixth College Commuter Center","subtitle":"Catalyst Building, North Torrey Pines Living and Learning Neighborhood","notes":"Use the computers, nearby printer access, kitchen facilities, and seating for a practical study break in the Sixth neighborhood.","short_summary":"A commuter center with computers, kitchen facilities, and lounge furniture.","evidence_claim":"UC San Diego places the Sixth College Commuter Center in the Catalyst Building basement and lists wireless internet, computers, printer access, kitchen facilities, and comfortable furniture.","source_url":"https://students.ucsd.edu/campus-services/parking-transportation/commuter/lounges.html","source_title":"Commuter Lounges","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-05-11","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The page lists it as open seven days a week, 8 a.m.–9 p.m.; confirm hours during holidays and breaks.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ucsd-angelas-space","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Angela’s Space","title":"Angela’s Space","subtitle":"Marshall College study space","notes":"Use the shared seating for an individual or small-group session, and check Marshall College information if your visit falls during a break.","short_summary":"A Marshall College study space explicitly open to all students.","evidence_claim":"UC San Diego lists Angela’s Space as a 50-seat Marshall College study space that is open to all students.","source_url":"https://students.ucsd.edu/campus-services/technology/campus-study-locations.html","source_title":"Where to Study on Campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-05-11","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Listed academic-quarter hours are 8 a.m.–11 p.m.; availability may change during finals, holidays, breaks, and summer.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
